      "side": 1,
      "message": "If you use `reflect.PtrTo(archVariantGroupStruct)` here the top level type will be a struct containing a single nil pointer, which will be very small.  Then blueprint will allocate the `archVariantGroupStruct` if the property is used, which avoids allocating the full `len(archNames) * len(dpiNames)` properties for every module.  You could do the same on lines 564 and 572.  You\u0027ll need to add nil checks when traversing the structs on line 176 though.",
